  "body": "Closes #864\nClaim: mac/M1\n\n**Problem.** The \"réponse postée avec succès\" confirmation stays on screen until the cross is tapped. The same happens with the banners after an edit, a delete, a new topic or a new MP.\n\n**Cause** (hypothesis, not reproduced on a device). The 4 s dismissal was a `Task.sleep` in each view's `.task(id:)`. For the reader, `ReaderReplyFlow` sits at the root of `TopicReaderView` (`TopicReaderView.swift:97`), so covering or rebuilding the view cancels the sleep, and the guard then returns without clearing. A timer owned by the model fixes it whatever the trigger, since it no longer depends on the view lifecycle.\n\n**Change.**\n- One shared `ConfirmationAutoDismiss`:\n  - a 4 s delay, with an injectable sleep;\n  - generation-guarded, so an old timer never clears a newer sentence.\n- It is owned by `TopicReaderModel`, `TopicListModel` and `MessageListModel`. It is armed when a success sentence is set and cancelled when the sentence is cleared.\n- The three view timers are removed.\n- Success sentences only: errors and unconfirmed messages never reach it.\n- The cross is unchanged.\n- Under VoiceOver nothing is armed, so the sentence stays until the cross. The issue asks that the auto-dismiss never cut the announcement short, and the system gives no reading-time value to wait for.\n- Legacy at 87fe0d1c has no auto-dismissing banner. The 4 s is a choice within the 3–5 s the issue allows.\n\n**Tests.**\n- `ConfirmationAutoDismissTests` (8). They run on a manual sleeper, with no wall-clock wait and with bounded waits. They cover:\n  - the delay is within range;\n  - the reply, topic and MP sentences clear after the delay;\n  - the cross wins over a stale timer;\n  - an old timer does not clear a newer confirmation;\n  - an unconfirmed reply arms nothing;\n  - with VoiceOver on, nothing is armed; with it off, the timer is armed.\n- They fail with the timer or the VoiceOver guard disabled, shown red on iPhone and iPad.\n- Full gate green on iPhone and iPad (1483 tests).\n\n**Not verified.** The cause above, and the behaviour under VoiceOver on a device.\n\n**Known low points (review round 2, not blocking).** Three tests read the host's real VoiceOver state: they assume it is off, as in CI. VoiceOver is read only when the timer is armed.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CJ1auuPWv2FeT7Q4Ps\n",
