   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5) — REQUEST CHANGES** — head 113d94fe (branch fix/864-reply-posted-autodismiss, before the PR)\n\n1. **medium** — `ConfirmationAutoDismiss.swift:10-30`: #864 asks that the auto-dismiss \"never cut the announcement short\" and follow the system's guidance when an accessibility setting needs the message to stay longer; nothing handles VoiceOver. Fix: skip `arm` (or lengthen the delay) while `UIAccessibility.isVoiceOverRunning`, tested through an injected flag; or defer it to an issue named in the PR.\n2. **low** — PR body \"Cause\": not shown for the reader (`ReaderReplyFlow` sits at the root of `TopicReaderView`, `TopicReaderView.swift:97`; a covered view restarts `.task(id:)` on reappear). State it as a hypothesis; the model-owned timer fixes it either way.\n3. **nit** — `ConfirmationAutoDismissTests.swift:86-100`: the list and MP checks call `finish` without `waitUntilAsked`; they pass only because `load` happens to suspend.\n4. **nit** — `ConfirmationAutoDismiss.swift:24`: `[weak self]` then `guard let self` keeps the timer alive through the sleep; harmless, but the weak capture does nothing.\n\nChecked and correct: `didSet` on these `@Observable` properties fires on every write path; no re-entry; the generation guard is needed and tested; removing the arm call from any model fails a test; only successes reach the timer; the announcement is unchanged; no view timer is left.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
