   "body": "**Adversarial review round 2 (Opus 5.5) — APPROVE** — head ee348d03 (round 1: REQUEST CHANGES at 113d94fe)\n\nRound-1 findings: 1 fixed (`ConfirmationAutoDismiss.swift:28`, no timer under VoiceOver), 2 fixed (cause stated as a hypothesis), 3 fixed (bounded waits, tests :91 and :99), 4 fixed (deliberately strong capture).\n\n1. **low** — `ConfirmationAutoDismissTests.swift:75, :87, :96`: three tests still read the real `UIAccessibility.isVoiceOverRunning`; with VoiceOver on in the host they would fail or pass for the wrong reason. Pin `isVoiceOverRunning = { false }` there. Not blocking.\n2. **low (optional)** — `ConfirmationAutoDismiss.swift:28`: VoiceOver is read at arm time only; turning it on during the 4 s still clears (nothing is cut short, the announcement was posted with it off); turning it off waits for the cross (the safe side). Observing `voiceOverStatusDidChangeNotification` would go further; the issue does not require it.\n\nSettled: the VoiceOver policy matches #864 and WCAG 2.2 SC 2.2.1 (iOS exposes no recommended timeout); no retain cycle beyond the delay (the models are captured weakly in `clear`); waits are bounded and the VoiceOver negative test is meaningful.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
